course: dictionary
lesson: 12912
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is used. The word established can mean set up for a long time, or started, or proved. «The bakery on the corner is well established; it has been there for fifty years.» Here established means set up and trusted for a long time.
explain: Established is also the past form of the verb establish. When it means started or created, the sentence will show something being set up. «The settlers established a town by the river.» The settlers started the town. «The scientists established that the water was clean.» The scientists proved it.
explain: To choose the right meaning, swap in a simple word such as «set up» or «proved» and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the meaning. Then check the clues around the word, such as years, towns or tests.
fact: Established means set up and existing for a long time, so people accept and trust it.
fact: As the past form of establish, established means started or created, such as a school, business or rule.
fact: Established can also mean proved or shown to be true, as in «established fact».
fact: A «well established» shop is one that has been there for years.
fact: An «established fact» is something that has been proved, often in science.
exercise: «The town was established by settlers in 1820.» What does established mean here? | Lost and forgotten | *Started or created | Painted bright red | Closed down for good
exercise: «The old library is well established and trusted by everyone in the village.» What does established mean? | *Set up and existing for a long time | Moved to another town | Brand new and untested | Hidden under the ground
exercise: «Scientists have established that bees can count.» Find and copy the word that tells you the scientists proved something. | bees | *established | count | scientists
test: «The club was established in 1950, and it still meets every Friday.» Which meaning fits best? | *Set up and started | Very noisy | Stopped for good | Painted over
test: Ben says, «It is an established fact that the Earth goes round the Sun.» What does established fact mean? | A fact that changes every day | *A fact that has been proved true | A made-up story | A fact nobody has heard of
exam: Which meaning of established fits «The shop is well established in the town»? | *Set up and existing for a long time | Hidden from view | Proved true | Started by a new owner today
